ISO 8601 grammar
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The grammar is based on the ISO 8601 grammar from the ANTLR grammars-v4
repository:

  Copyright (C) 2020 by Student Main
  License: 0BSD
  Source:  https://github.com/antlr/grammars-v4/blob/753536777d827ccc0c9b108531ea67375c2039ac/iso8601/iso8601.g4

Modifications Copyright (C) 2024-2026 Nvaria GmbH, also released under 0BSD:

  - Renamed the grammar from iso8601 to Iso8601 to follow Java class naming.
  - recurringCount accepts R-1 (unbounded) besides R and Rn. The minus is a
    separate token so that it does not clash with dates such as 2026-09-15.
  - New entry rule dateOrDatetime: a date and time, or a date alone.
  - New rules intervalPointBasic and intervalPointExtended: the start of a
    start/duration interval and the end of a duration/end interval may be a
    date alone, not only a date and time.
  - intervalYMDTimeBasic tries monthDateBasic after the date alternatives, so
    an ambiguous basic-format value such as 0203 is read as a reduced-precision
    date rather than month and day.
  - Removed the duplicate monthDateExtended alternative from
    intervalYMDTimeExtended.


